after 1991, but the size of the reform's own contribution is argued over. One school dates the trend break to the 1980s, when a milder pro-business shift was already under way, and treats 1991 as consolidation of a trend rather than its start. Others argue the 1980s expansion was debt-financed and unsustainable, and that 1991 is what made growth durable.","refs":"[\"Government of India, Union Budget speech, 24 July 1991\", \"Rodrik & Subramanian, 'From Hindu Growth to Productivity Surge' (IMF Staff Papers, 2005)\", \"Panagariya, 'India: The Emerging Giant' (2008)\"]"},{"iso3":"IND","date":"1996-04-01","year":1996,"kind":"power_transfer","title":"Legislative election - power changes hands","detail":"Vote, As Scheduled","source":"REIGN election list","source_url":"https://oefdatascience.github.io/REIGN.github.io/","historical":false,"contested":null,"refs":null},{"iso3":"IND","date":"1996-05-16","year":1996,"kind":"leader_change","title":"Vajpayee takes power","detail":"Change of national leader.","source":"REIGN leader list","source_url":"https://oefdatascience.github.io/REIGN.github.io/","historical":false,"contested":null,"refs":null},{"iso3":"IND","date":"1996-06-01","year":1996,"kind":"leader_change","title":"Gowda takes power","detail":"Change of national leader.","source":"REIGN leader list","source_url":"https://oefdatascience.github.io/REIGN.github.io/","historical":false,"contested":null,"refs":null},{"iso3":"IND","date":"1997-04-21","year":1997,"kind":"leader_change","title":"Gujral takes power","detail":"Change of national leader.","source":"REIGN leader list","source_url":"https://oefdatascience.github.io/REIGN.github.io/","historical":false,"contested":null,"refs":null},{"iso3":"IND","date":"1998-02-01","year":1998,"kind":"power_transfer","title":"Legislative election - power changes hands","detail":"Vote, Early","source":"REIGN election list","source_url":"https://oefdatascience.github.io/REIGN.github.io/","historical":false,"contested":null,"refs":null